  "content": {
    "id": "p74-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "The height of a tree after $t$ years is given by $\\dfrac{dQ}{dt}=0.03Q(45-Q)$.\n\nThe tree is $0.3$ m high when it is planted.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p74-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Evaluate $a$ and $b$ if $\\dfrac{1}{Q(45-Q)}=\\dfrac{a}{Q}+\\dfrac{b}{45-Q}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=\\dfrac{1}{45},\\quad b=\\dfrac{1}{45}$.",
          "worked": "Multiply both sides by $Q(45-Q)$:\n$$1=a(45-Q)+bQ.$$\nSubstitute $Q=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}1&=45a\\\\a&=\\frac{1}{45}.\\end{aligned}$$\nSubstitute $Q=45$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}1&=45b\\\\b&=\\frac{1}{45}.\\end{aligned}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\frac{1}{Q(45-Q)}=\\frac{1}{45}\\left(\\frac{1}{Q}+\\frac{1}{45-Q}\\right).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p74-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Solve the differential equation to find the formula for the height of the tree.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$Q=\\dfrac{45}{1+149e^{-1.35t}}$ metres, where $t\\geq0$.",
          "worked": "Separate variables:\n$$\\frac{1}{Q(45-Q)}\\,dQ=0.03\\,dt.$$\nUsing partial fractions from (a):\n$$\\frac{1}{45}\\left(\\frac{1}{Q}+\\frac{1}{45-Q}\\right)\\,dQ=0.03\\,dt.$$\nIntegrate both sides and combine the logarithms:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{45}\\left(\\ln|Q|-\\ln|45-Q|\\right)&=0.03t+C_1\\\\\\ln\\left|\\frac{Q}{45-Q}\\right|&=1.35t+C_2\\\\\\frac{Q}{45-Q}&=Ae^{1.35t}.\\end{aligned}$$\nSubstitute $Q=0.3$ when $t=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{0.3}{44.7}&=A\\\\A&=\\frac{1}{149}.\\end{aligned}$$\nHence,\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Q}{45-Q}&=\\frac{1}{149}e^{1.35t}\\\\149Q&=(45-Q)e^{1.35t}\\\\149Q+Qe^{1.35t}&=45e^{1.35t}\\\\Q(149+e^{1.35t})&=45e^{1.35t}\\\\Q&=\\frac{45e^{1.35t}}{149+e^{1.35t}}.\\end{aligned}$$\nDivide the numerator and denominator by $e^{1.35t}$:\n$$Q=\\frac{45}{1+149e^{-1.35t}}\\text{ metres},\\qquad t\\geq0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 101
      },
      {
        "id": "p74-q12-c",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find its height after the following times. Give your answers to 2 decimal places.",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p74-q12-c-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "2 years",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$4.09$ m.",
              "worked": "Substitute $t=2$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}Q(2)&=\\frac{45}{1+149e^{-1.35(2)}}\\\\&=\\frac{45}{1+149e^{-2.7}}\\\\&\\approx4.09\\text{ m}.\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 19
          },
          {
            "id": "p74-q12-c-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "8 years",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$44.86$ m.",
              "worked": "Substitute $t=8$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}Q(8)&=\\frac{45}{1+149e^{-1.35(8)}}\\\\&=\\frac{45}{1+149e^{-10.8}}\\\\&\\approx44.86\\text{ m}.\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 19
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p74-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "What is its ultimate height?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$45$ m.",
          "worked": "As $t\\to\\infty$, $e^{-1.35t}\\to0$, so\n$$Q\\to\\frac{45}{1+0}=45.$$\nThe ultimate height is $45$ m.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      }
    ]
  },
